      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_n4u6Z3zp6kdRyYXwJSUPXd9dt9s-CbKXE9WwwClaiqUHc=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Inspiring country. Visited Managua, but not nearly long enough stay. Worked with many Nicaraguans, who helped teach me to speak Spanish (along with Cubans). Nice and polite people, gorgeous woman, delicious cuisine. Flor de Caña Siete Años Ron is delicious, especially for the price. Aldi Supermarket sells Whole Bean Nicaraguan Coffee. The government/politics has challenges. One woman I knew had her house and farm In Nicaragua taken over by Sandinista “remnants” and had to get the military to evict them. If you can’t visit Nicaragua, but are in Miami, dine at Los Ranchos, a Nicaraguan Steak House. Fantastic Churasco and Chimichurri! ¡Buen Provecho! Excellent video! Thanks!",
      "likeCount": 2,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-11T01:37:26Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
